blackcrate
===========

Category-wise installation checker for offensive security tools.


OVERVIEW
--------
  blackcrate scans your system category-wise and reports what's installed
  and what's missing across your entire offensive security toolkit.
  Designed for pentesters and red teamers who want a quick situational
  awareness check before jumping into an engagement.


USAGE
-----
  chmod +x blackcrate.sh
  ./blackcrate.sh


OUTPUT
------
  ==================== Web Application ====================
    [✔] ffuf: installed
    [✔] sqlmap: installed
    [✘] dalfox: not installed

  ==================== Wordlists & Payloads ====================
    [✔] wordlists/: dir exists
    [✔] rockyou.txt: file exists
    [✘] seclists/: not found


CATEGORIES
----------
  Reconnaissance - Passive      whois, amass, subfinder, shodan, censys
  Reconnaissance - Active       nmap, masscan, nuclei, nikto, sslscan
  Web Application               burpsuite, ffuf, sqlmap, caido, dalfox
  Password & Hash Attacks       hashcat, john, hydra, cewl, crunch
  Exploitation                  msfconsole, msfvenom, searchsploit
  Active Directory & Windows    impacket suite, bloodhound, crackmapexec, evil-winrm
  Linux Privilege Escalation    peass-ng, lse.sh, pspy
  Windows Privilege Escalation  peass-ng, wesng
  Network & Traffic             wireshark, responder, bettercap, mitm6
  Post Exploitation & C2        sliver, havoc, empire
  Pivoting & Tunneling          chisel, ligolo-ng, proxychains, socat
  Wireless                      aircrack-ng, hcxdumptool, wifite, kismet
  Reverse Engineering           ghidra, radare2, gdb, binwalk
  Forensics & Steganography     volatility3, steghide, zsteg, autopsy
  Encoding & Crypto             openssl, base64, xxd
  Wordlists & Payloads          wordlists, seclists, rockyou
  Utility & Workflow            tmux, curl, jq, python3


DETECTION
---------
  binaries / cli tools       command -v + whereis -b
  scripts / files            find by filename (.sh, .py, .txt, etc.)
  directories                find by directory name (trailing /)


